### FixIt Backend API — Manual Test Requests
### Open this file with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and click
### "Send Request" above each block, top to bottom (some requests depend
### on tokens/IDs captured from earlier ones via REST Client's variables).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

### 1. Register a new customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Customer",
  "email": "customer@example.com",
  "password": "Test@123456",
  "role": "customer"
}

### 2. Register a new professional
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Electrician",
  "email": "pro@example.com",
  "password": "Test@123456",
  "role": "professional"
}

### 3. Attempt to register as admin (should be blocked / downgraded — never actually admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Security Test User",
  "email": "securitytest@example.com",
  "password": "Test@123456",
  "role": "admin"
}

### 4. Login as the customer (captures token for later requests)
# @name customerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@example.com",
  "password": "Test@123456"
}

### 5. Login as the professional (captures token for later requests)
# @name proLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "pro@example.com",
  "password": "Test@123456"
}

### 6. Login with wrong password (should be 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 7. Get all professionals — public, no token needed
GET {{baseUrl}}/professionals

### 8. Try creating a professional listing with NO token (should be 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/professionals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "No Auth Test",
  "service": "Electrical",
  "description": "Should be rejected",
  "location": "Bengaluru",
  "price": 500
}

### 9. Try creating a professional listing as a CUSTOMER (should be 403 — wrong role)
POST {{baseUrl}}/professionals
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Customer Trying To Create",
  "service": "Electrical",
  "description": "Should be rejected — customers can't create listings",
  "location": "Bengaluru",
  "price": 500
}

### 10. Create a professional listing as the PROFESSIONAL (should succeed — 201)
# @name createProfessional
POST {{baseUrl}}/professionals
Authorization: Bearer {{proLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Electrician",
  "service": "Electrical",
  "description": "Experienced electrician for home electrical repairs",
  "location": "Bengaluru",
  "rating": 4.5,
  "price": 500,
  "availability": true
}

### 11. Get the newly created professional by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/professionals/{{createProfessional.response.body.$.professional._id}}

### 12. Update the listing as its OWNER (should succeed)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/professionals/{{createProfessional.response.body.$.professional._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{proLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 600,
  "availability": false
}

### 13. Register + log in a SECOND professional, to test ownership enforcement
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Second Professional",
  "email": "pro2@example.com",
  "password": "Test@123456",
  "role": "professional"
}

### 14. Log in as the second professional
# @name proLogin2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "pro2@example.com",
  "password": "Test@123456"
}

### 15. Second professional tries to update the FIRST professional's listing (should be 403)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/professionals/{{createProfessional.response.body.$.professional._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{proLogin2.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 1
}

### 16. Create a booking as the customer, against the professional's listing
# @name createBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "professional": "{{createProfessional.response.body.$.professional._id}}",
  "service": "Electrical",
  "date": "2026-10-05",
  "time": "11:00 AM",
  "status": "pending"
}

### 17. Get all bookings for the logged-in customer
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 18. Get one booking by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.$.booking._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 19. Update the booking (owner)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.$.booking._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "confirmed"
}

### 20. Second professional tries to view the booking (should be 404 — hidden, not theirs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.$.booking._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{proLogin2.response.body.$.token}}

### 21. Try getting bookings with NO token (should be 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings

### 22. Registration validation — invalid email, short password (should be 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "A",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123"
}

### 23. Professional validation — missing/invalid fields (should be 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/professionals
Authorization: Bearer {{proLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "service": "",
  "description": "",
  "location": "",
  "price": -100,
  "rating": 8,
  "availability": "maybe"
}

### 24. Booking validation — invalid ID and bad status (should be 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "professional": "invalid-id",
  "service": "",
  "date": "",
  "time": "",
  "status": "wrong-status"
}

### 25. Invalid MongoDB ID format on professional lookup (should be 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/professionals/invalid-id

### 26. Delete the booking (owner cleans up after testing)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.$.booking._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 27. Delete the professional listing (owner cleans up after testing)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/professionals/{{createProfessional.response.body.$.professional._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{proLogin.response.body.$.token}}